Lets the scan fast path take a symlink as unchanged when its kind matches
the index, whatever its target, as before 34b5d6f (§7.3), so a retarget
whose watcher event was dropped is invisible to every later scan. Only
Entry::unchanged_by_stat, the fast path's test, changes: the commit guard
keeps comparing the target.

test: delocal-sim regressions::a_retargeted_symlink_the_watcher_missed_is_found_by_the_next_scan
test: delocal-engine entry::tests::the_fast_path_compares_kind_size_mtime_exec_and_symlink_target

diff --git a/crates/engine/src/entry.rs b/crates/engine/src/entry.rs
index 864d5c4..6e38914 100644
--- a/crates/engine/src/entry.rs
+++ b/crates/engine/src/entry.rs
@@ -155,7 +155,11 @@ impl Entry {
     /// [`Observed::unchanged_by_stat`]. A tombstone matches nothing:
     /// whatever is on disk is new.
     pub fn unchanged_by_stat(&self, seen: &Observed) -> bool {
-        !self.deleted && self.observed().unchanged_by_stat(seen)
+        let seen = Observed {
+            hash: self.hash,
+            ..seen.clone()
+        };
+        !self.deleted && self.observed().unchanged_by_stat(&seen)
     }
 
     /// A metadata-only change (§7.1): the content is what it was before.
